DEVICE SPIKE

# Robot Lab: a drawing robot.
# Model: Drawing robot (the SPIKE driving base, wheels on A and B; its castor ball is
# marked "Draws on the floor", so it draws a line wherever it rolls).
# Four times: drive 20 cm, then turn a quarter on the spot. That is a square.
# The ball sits behind the wheels, so at each corner its line swings round in a loop.
# A turn goes on a little after the gyro passes the mark: the program sees the yaw
# once a frame, and the robot needs a moment to stop. So it turns quickly to 70°,
# then slowly to 89°, where it stops at about 90°. (Stopping at once from full
# speed overshoots by 6 or 7 degrees, and the square does not close.)
# Try a triangle: 3 times, a third of a turn (120°) each.
WHEN flag clicked:
  set movement motors A B
  set movement speed 30
  REPEAT 4:
    move forward 20 cm
    reset yaw
    start tank 20 -20
    wait until (spike angle yaw) > 70
    start tank 5 -5
    wait until (spike angle yaw) > 89
    stop movement
    wait 0.3 seconds
